From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 07:46:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 090/118] Reading a variable's bits through PT(@v)^ does not
 force v into memory

PInt64(@d)^ is the usual way to read the bits of a Double (sign of -0.0,
NaN boxing, hashing), but taking the address made d non-regable for the
whole routine, so each value stored to it went through a store and a reload.
taddrnode now leaves @v of a scalar local or by-value parameter pending
(anf_bitcast_pending), and once the routine is parsed, before its inline
info is copied, optbitcast.resolve_pending_bitcasts turns every PT(@v)^ that
is only read, with T a scalar of v's size, into an internal tc_equal
conversion of v (second_nothing moves an xmm register to an integer one for
it); every other @v (written, passed by reference, an inline node argument,
the plain pointer) makes v non-regable as before. tests/test/opt/tbitcast1.pp.
---
 compiler/nmem.pas           |  12 +-
 compiler/optbitcast.pas     | 238 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 compiler/psub.pas           |   6 +-
 tests/test/opt/tbitcast1.pp | 114 +++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 366 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 compiler/optbitcast.pas
 create mode 100644 tests/test/opt/tbitcast1.pp

